{%- comment -%}
  ADAPTER: Wishlist cross-device sync swap point.

  Current state (native, no app): assets/wishlist-store.js keeps the
  guest wishlist entirely in localStorage (Nexoira.wishlist.*). It works
  today with zero setup, but does not sync across devices or survive a
  cleared browser, and there is no storefront-side write API for
  persisting it to the customer's account without a backend.

  To add real cross-device sync + guest-to-account merge on login
  (PRD §12):
    1. Pick a backend: a customer metafield written via a Shopify
       Function/app proxy, or a third-party wishlist app.
    2. In assets/wishlist-store.js, change `read()`/`write()` to call
       that backend's API instead of localStorage, keeping the same
       Nexoira.wishlist.getAll/has/add/remove/toggle interface so every
       caller (wishlist-button.liquid, the card, the PDP) needs no
       changes.
    3. On login, merge: read the local guest list once, push it to the
       account-backed store, then switch reads/writes to the backend.
    4. Guest checkout and browsing must keep working if that backend is
       unreachable - wrap calls in try/catch and fall back to the
       existing localStorage behavior, never block Add to Cart.
{%- endcomment -%}
